<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility — Freighthub"
  description="How Freighthub is built for accessibility: semantic HTML, keyboard support, contrast, no autoplay, known limitations and how to report a barrier."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Accessibility</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">Last reviewed 15 November 2026</p>

    <p class="lede">
      The site is built to be readable without a mouse, without colour, and without the images. This
      page states what is done, what is not perfect, and how to report a barrier.
    </p>

    <h2>Standard targeted</h2>
    <p>
      The aim is WCAG 2.2 level AA for the content pages. That is a target, not a certification: no
      external audit has been carried out, and the site does not claim conformance it has not tested.
    </p>

    <h2>What is in place</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Semantic HTML: one <code>h1</code> per page, headings in order, lists for lists, tables with header cells and captions where a table carries data.</li>
      <li>Keyboard access: navigation and links are reachable and visible on focus; no custom widget traps focus.</li>
      <li>Contrast: body text and links are chosen to meet AA against their background.</li>
      <li>No autoplay, no carousels, no motion that cannot be stopped.</li>
      <li>Text is not locked to images; pages remain readable at 200% zoom and with images disabled.</li>
      <li>Language is declared as English, so screen readers do not mispronounce the page.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Wide data tables scroll horizontally on narrow screens; the content is available but the reading experience is cramped below 400 px.</li>
      <li>Some external documents linked from the site (regulator PDFs) are outside our control and may not be tagged for accessibility.</li>
      <li>Chinese characters and Arabic port names appear in some pages; pronunciation depends on the screen reader's language data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reporting a barrier</h2>
    <p>
      Write to <a href="mailto:editor@freighthub.net">editor@freighthub.net</a> with the page URL and
      what happened. Accessibility fixes are treated as corrections and dated on the page when the
      change is material.
    </p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <p><a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms of use</a> · <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
